From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:11:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] addons: an add-on naming both the AppCompat GUID and the
 toolkit is matched by the entry that fits

matchingTargetApplication prefers, in order: this application's own id, the
AppCompat GUID (extensions.guid.appCompatId, the Firefox GUID), the toolkit.
The AppCompat entry was taken whenever present, whatever its version range.

An add-on can name both for different reasons: the GUID entry for the
application that owns that GUID, at that application's versions (Basilisk is
{ec8030f7-...} at 52.9.x), and a toolkit entry meaning "any other application
on this platform". For an application that is neither, with an AppCompat
version of 56.9, the GUID entry "52.9.0 - 52.9.*" under strict compatibility
does not fit - and because it was preferred, the toolkit entry that does
describe the application was never looked at. The add-on was installed and
immediately disabled as incompatible.

Now the AppCompat entry is used only if it admits the AppCompat version (both
bounds under strict compatibility, the lower bound otherwise - the rule
isCompatibleWith applies) or if there is no toolkit entry to fall back to.
Nothing changes for an add-on that names one of the two, or whose GUID entry
fits.

Found with Palefill 1.30 (toolkit@mozilla.org 4.8.2 - 10.*, platform 6.9.0),
which now installs enabled and applies its fixes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LcrVQFRMC2ANGDfVaRG9Ed
---
 .../extensions/internal/XPIProvider.jsm       | 28 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIProvider.jsm b/toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIProvider.jsm
index 1b23267764..552a6266d8 100644
--- a/toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIProvider.jsm
+++ b/toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIProvider.jsm
@@ -6432,8 +6432,19 @@ AddonInternal.prototype = {
     // Only do this for extensions. Other types should not be allowed.
     if (this.type == "extension") {
       for (let targetApp of this.targetApplications) {
-        if (targetApp.id == APPCOMPATID) // AppCompat GUID
+        if (targetApp.id == APPCOMPATID) { // AppCompat GUID
+          // An add-on may name BOTH the AppCompat GUID and the toolkit: the GUID entry
+          // written for the application that owns that GUID, at that application's
+          // versions, and the toolkit entry for "any other application on this platform".
+          // Taking the GUID entry regardless disabled exactly the add-ons that had gone
+          // to the trouble of declaring generic platform support (one whose GUID entry
+          // says 52.9.*, against an AppCompat version of 56.9). Where the GUID entry does
+          // not fit this application's AppCompat version and a toolkit entry was given,
+          // the toolkit entry is the one that describes us.
+          if (app && !this._fitsAppCompat(targetApp))
+            break;
           return targetApp;
+        }
       }
     }
 #endif
@@ -6441,6 +6452,21 @@ AddonInternal.prototype = {
     return app;
   },
 
+#ifdef UXP_APPCOMPAT_GUID
+  // Whether aTargetApp (an AppCompat GUID entry) admits this application's AppCompat
+  // version, by the same rule isCompatibleWith applies: both bounds under strict
+  // compatibility, the lower bound alone otherwise.
+  _fitsAppCompat: function AddonInternal_fitsAppCompat(aTargetApp) {
+    let strict = !(this.type in COMPATIBLE_BY_DEFAULT_TYPES) ||
+                 AddonManager.strictCompatibility || this.strictCompatibility ||
+                 this.hasBinaryComponents;
+    if (Services.vc.compare(APPCOMPATVERSION, aTargetApp.minVersion) < 0)
+      return false;
+    return !strict || Services.vc.compare(APPCOMPATVERSION, aTargetApp.maxVersion) <= 0;
+  },
+#endif
+
+
   get blocklistState() {
     let staticItem = findMatchingStaticBlocklistItem(this);
     if (staticItem)
